course: dictionary
lesson: 8494
title: The past of sing: sang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sang is the past form of sing. Use it for something that already happened: «We sang happy birthday» means the singing is finished. Sing, sang, sung is an irregular verb, so it does not add -ed.
explain: «The birds sang at dawn.» Birds sing, and so do other things. When a kettle boils, it can sing, which means it makes a high, musical sound. Sang can describe a voice, a bird, a kettle or the wind.
explain: In maths, «The choir sang 4 songs, each 3 minutes long» means 4 × 3 = 12 minutes of singing. The clue is in the numbers, so you can work out the total.
fact: Sang is the past simple form of sing: sing (now), sang (before), sung (after have).
fact: «I sang» stands alone, but «I have sung» needs have before it, just like «I swam» and «I have swum».
fact: «Sang» means made musical sounds with the voice, or made a high, musical sound (birds, kettles, wind).
fact: Sing, sang, sung; ring, rang, rung; and swim, swam, swum are irregular verbs that come in little families.
fact: «Sang someone's praises» means said very good things about them.
exercise: Yesterday we ___ happy birthday to Nan. | sing | *sang | singing | sung
exercise: «The kettle sang when it boiled.» What does sang mean here? | Ran away | *Made a high, musical sound | Fell over | Went quiet
exercise: Finish the sentence: «I have ___ in the choir all year.» | singing | sang | sing | *sung
test: «The choir sang 4 songs, each 3 minutes long.» How many minutes did they sing altogether? | *12 | 3 | 7 | 16
test: Which sentence is correct? | I have sing at the fair. | *I have sung at the fair. | I have singing at the fair. | I have sang at the fair.
exam: Which sentence uses sang correctly? | The birds sing at dawn yesterday. | The birds sung at dawn. | The birds have sang at dawn. | *The birds sang at dawn.
